{"id":4124,"date":"2024-02-14T09:42:50","date_gmt":"2024-02-14T09:42:50","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/?p=4124"},"modified":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","modified_gmt":"2024-12-10T12:23:16","slug":"the-linbury-trust-supports-ccac-in-promoting-emergent-designers","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/the-linbury-trust-supports-ccac-in-promoting-emergent-designers\/","title":{"rendered":"The Linbury Trust supports CCAC in promoting emergent designers"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3441 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-356x200.jpg 356w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Aurelie-200x113.jpg 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/576;\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em><sub>Aur\u00e9lie Fontan led a co-design collaboration on sustainable fashion in 2022, covering topics such as plant-leather based alternative Mycelium. Her eponymous label, established in 2018, goes from strength to strength<\/sub><\/em><\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>CCAC is creating a new \u201cemergent designers\u201d stream, which over the coming months will support five rising designers to work with us on our co-design projects. <\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To date, CCAC\u2019s school projects have blossomed with the help of young, emergent designers. Four of our partner designers in 2022\/2023 were from fledgling practices. Their CCAC programmes covered a cross-section of design disciplines and subjects: timber architecture, fashion and clothing, ecology and landscape, and design for an urban community, all projected to 2050 in extreme climatic conditions. To the joy of Yr5 school children, our emerging designers brought a pioneering spirit, the ability to innovate, and unbounded enthusiasm.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now many of CCAC\u2019s design partners generously give their time for free. But we recognise that young, independent designers from under-represented groups or from small, newly established practices lack the resources to do so. The Linbury Trust\u2019s assistance will support these designers to work with us, enabling CCAC to further consolidate our projects in state schools, while continuing to support incipient talent.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">We will shortly be launching a call for emergent designers to apply to The CCAC Young Designer Award, supported by the Linbury Trust. <\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-3550 lazyload\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-1536x864.jpg 1536w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-2048x1152.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-356x200.jpg 356w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2023\/07\/Finn-and-Jack_-Forest-Day.00_07_53_05.Still006-200x113.jpg 200w\" data-sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" src=\"data:image\/svg+xml;base64,PHN2ZyB3aWR0aD0iMSIgaGVpZ2h0PSIxIiB4bWxucz0iaHR0cDovL3d3dy53My5vcmcvMjAwMC9zdmciPjwvc3ZnPg==\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/576;\" \/><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\"><em><sub>Jack Cardno takes the Ashton Gate children into the woods for a Forest Future introductory lesson<\/sub><\/em><\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https:\/\/linburytrust.org.uk\/\">The Linbury Trust<\/a> is a long-established grant-maker in the arts and culture sectors. They also support projects focused on education, the environment and climate. The Trust was set up in 1973 by Lord Sainsbury of Preston Candover KG and his wife Lady Sainsbury CBE, Anya Linden. CCAC is immensely grateful for The Linbury Trust\u2019s support.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"434\" data-src=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Linbury-colour-1024x434.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-4108 lazyload\" style=\"--smush-placeholder-width: 1024px; --smush-placeholder-aspect-ratio: 1024\/434;width:214px;height:auto\" data-srcset=\"https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Linbury-colour-1024x434.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/Linbury-colour-300x127.jpg 300w, https:\/\/cc-ac.org\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/0